<commits>
1b481e56a2 test: characterize RPC and wallet input logs

Co-authored-by: Russell Yanofsky <russ@yanofsky.org>

5dff09c040 log: split multiline messages

Add SplitLines and use it for intentional multiline exception, message-box, wallet transaction, and wallet database output. Giving each line its own log entry preserves readability when embedded newlines are escaped by the logger.

Visit line views synchronously through a callback to avoid allocating a container.

Log exceptions as ordinary warnings and remove the blank lines and asterisk banner. Each line now has the usual warning prefix, so the separators add noise without diagnostic information. Keep the existing stderr formatting.

Split wallet database errors too, so descriptor-load diagnostics and their Details line remain separately readable.

Co-authored-by: Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com>

0321f72012 log: escape newlines in messages

Escape embedded newlines as \x0a, like other control characters, so user input cannot forge additional log lines. Apply this in the logger to cover RPC methods, wallet names, and other runtime strings. Preserve non-ASCII bytes so valid UTF-8 remains readable.

Remove exactly one trailing newline before escaping because many callers still supply it as the conventional log terminator. Append the terminator centrally, escaping any remaining newlines.

A follow-up could remove conventional trailing newlines from logging call sites and then remove the suffix stripping here.
</commits>

